%%
pst-fit.sty ----------- (hv)
0.01 2012-04-01  first CTAN version


pst-fit.tex ----------- (bl/hv)
0.04  2026-11-20  - new option plottype: confidence interval of the fit
                    (upperci, lowerci, bothci), prediction interval
                    (upperpi, lowerpi, bothpi) and standardised residuals
                  - new option printconfig: print the regression statistics
                    (t value, degrees of freedom, Sxx, Syy, Sxy, Syx, mean
                    values, half width of the confidence interval)
                  - new option tvp: Student t value for the intervals
                  - new option plotcoord: plot and statistics in the
                    transformed coordinates (trans) or with the statistics
                    of the untransformed data (special)
                  - new plot style ErrorFunction with the options xerrfunc
                    and yerrfunc: error bars with a calculated length
                  - R^2 is now calculated from the transformed data for all
                    fit functions; it was wrong for PowerFit, ExpFit,
                    GaussFit, CustomFit and for fits with a given Yint
                  - Yint is now respected by LogTFit, LogEFit and RecipFit
                  - terms with a coefficient of zero are no longer printed
                  - plotNoTwo works with plotNoMax=1
0.03  2024-03-17  - added option comma for decimals instead of dot 
0.02  2017-08-24  - use always URW fonts instead of PostScript, 
                    eg Helvetica->NimbusSanL
0.01  2012-04-01  - first CTAN version


